  "notes": "STIBOR transition to SWESTR was abandoned spring 2025 - 3M STIBOR remains the standard. Single-curve self-discounting default. OIS re-wired 2026-08-03 onto the SKSWS 'SEK SWESTR OIS' family (1W-20Y incl. every month to 11M and 18M) - the old SKSWTN family VERIFIED as legacy T/N (STINA): its 1M printed 1.766 vs SWESTR 1.655 and SKSWS1Z 1.650, ~+11bp of T/N basis, and it had NO sub-1Y quotes wired, so the OIS front extrapolated FLAT at the 1Y rate - the Riksbank meeting run's curve-implied rows read 2.076 for every front period against meeting tickers at 1.65-1.85. SKSWSE (5M, maturing over year-end) prints a real year-turn dip. SKSF4A ('4TH RIKS') publishes a live two-sided misprint (1.387 between 1.848/2.086 neighbours, 2026-08-03) - the meetings board's 20bp curve-sanity guard rejects it, labelled. IMM FRA strip SKF30001-SKF30901 added 2026-07 (SEK FRA 3M, live, dates from MATURITY) - shapes the STIBOR front end; expired/clashing contracts skipped by the bootstrapper. SEK IRS forward reference added 2026-07-30: SKFS year-pair securities (SKFS0505 BLC = 5y5y). Previously SEK had NO forward reference at all, so auditfwd could not see it."
